    <!--
      The paid unlock. Only the tile types in PAID_TILE_TYPES are affected, and the wording keeps
      to what is true: viewing a tile of a paid type always works, including one that arrived in a
      backup from somebody else. What is being sold is making them.

      Prefixed `purchase_` and not `unlock_`: `view_unlock_*` above is the parent-view PIN, and two
      unrelated things both called "unlock" in one string file is how the wrong one gets shown.
    -->
    <string name="edit_type_locked">Needs the full version</string>
    <!-- The button the offer folds down to. It sits over the fields of a locked tile type,
         which stay readable behind it: the point is to be able to see what a Video tile
         asks for before deciding whether it is worth paying for. -->
    <string name="purchase_show">Locked — tap to unlock</string>
    <string name="purchase_title">The full version</string>
